{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Natural Language Inference \u2014 Textual Entailment Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: run a pretrained NLI model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nli = pipeline(\"text-classification\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "               model=\"facebook/bart-large-mnli\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "               top_k=None)  # return all labels; replaces deprecated return_all_scores=True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "premise = \"The cat is sleeping on the couch.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "hypothesis = \"There is a cat in the room.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result = nli({\"text\": premise, \"text_pair\": hypothesis})[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(result)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# [{'label': 'entailment', 'score': 0.97},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#  {'label': 'neutral', 'score': 0.02},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#  {'label': 'contradiction', 'score': 0.01}]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For production NLI, `facebook/bart-large-mnli` and `microsoft/deberta-v3-large-mnli` are the open defaults. DeBERTa-v3 tops leaderboards."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: zero-shot classification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "zs = pipeline(\"zero-shot-classification\", model=\"facebook/bart-large-mnli\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "text = \"The stock market rallied after the central bank cut interest rates.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "labels = [\"finance\", \"sports\", \"politics\", \"technology\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result = zs(text, candidate_labels=labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(result)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# {'labels': ['finance', 'politics', 'technology', 'sports'],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#  'scores': [0.92, 0.05, 0.02, 0.01]}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The template is \"This example is about {label}.\" by default. Customize with `hypothesis_template`. No training data required. No fine-tuning. Works out of the box."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: faithfulness check for RAG"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def is_faithful(answer, context, threshold=0.5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = nli({\"text\": context, \"text_pair\": answer})[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    entail = next(s for s in result if s[\"label\"] == \"entailment\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return entail[\"score\"] > threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is the core of RAGAS faithfulness. Split the generated answer into atomic claims. Check each claim against the retrieved context. Report the fraction that entail."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: hand-rolled NLI classifier (conceptual)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py` for a stdlib-only toy: premise and hypothesis are compared via lexical overlap + negation detection. Not competitive with transformer models \u2014 but it shows the shape of the task: two texts in, 3-way label out, loss = cross-entropy over `{entail, contradict, neutral}`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `facebook/bart-large-mnli` on 20 hand-crafted (premise, hypothesis, label) triples covering all three classes. Measure accuracy. Add adversarial \"subsequence heuristic\" traps (\"I did not eat the cake\" vs \"I ate the cake\") and see if it breaks.\n2. **Medium.** Compare the zero-shot template `\"This text is about {label}\"` against `\"The topic is {label}\"` and `\"{label}\"` on 100 AG News headlines. Report accuracy swing.\n3. **Hard.** Build a RAG faithfulness checker: atomic-claim decomposition + NLI per claim. Evaluate on 50 RAG-generated answers with gold context. Measure false-positive and false-negative rates vs hand labels."
      ]
    }
  ],
